          "fact": "F2",
          "source": "thm-xd-finite-state-projection-loss-and-observable-bound",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $X_t$ be a given nonexplosive countable chain with rates $q(x,y)$, initial law $p_0$, and finite exit rates as in [[def-xd-countable-nonexplosive-ctmc]]. For a finite nonempty $F\\subseteq S$, let $\\tau_F$ and $Y_t$ be the killed projection of [[def-xd-finite-state-projection-and-cemetery-lift]]. Write $p_t(x)=\\mathbb P(X_t=x)$ and $u_F(t,x)=\\mathbb P(Y_t=x)$ for $x\\in F$. Then\n\n$$u_F(t,x)=\\mathbb P(X_t=x,\\tau_F>t)\\le p_t(x),\\qquad c_F(t)=\\mathbb P(\\tau_F\\le t).$$\n\nIf $\\bar u_F$ is $u_F$ extended by zero to $S\\setminus F$, then\n\n$$\\|p_t-\\bar u_F(t)\\|_{\\ell^1(S)}=c_F(t).$$\n\nFor any bounded real observable $f:S\\to\\mathbb R$, put $\\operatorname{osc}(f):=\\sup_{x\\in S}f(x)-\\inf_{x\\in S}f(x)$ and extend it to the cemetery state by $f(\\dagger):=(\\sup f+\\inf f)/2$. The corresponding expectation error obeys\n\n$$|\\mathbb E[f(X_t)]-\\mathbb E[f(Y_t)]|\\le\\tfrac12\\operatorname{osc}(f)c_F(t).$$\n\nThe finite cemetery lift $\\widetilde Q_F$ in [[def-xd-finite-state-projection-and-cemetery-lift]] is a finite generator and $\\mathcal L(Y_t)=e^{t\\widetilde Q_F}\\mathcal L(Y_0)$. A path that exits $F$ and later returns contributes to the full marginal but remains at the cemetery state in the killed projection.",
          "uses": [
            "2.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F3",
          "source": "thm-xd-uniformization-truncation-and-error",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $Q$ be a finite column generator, $p_0$ a column probability vector, and $\\nu>0$ an admissible rate. For $\\lambda=\\nu t$ and $K\\ge0$, the exact one-series partial sum\n\n$$u_K(t):=\\sum_{k=0}^{K}e^{-\\lambda}\\frac{\\lambda^k}{k!}P^kp_0$$\n\nis nonnegative and substochastic, and its exact $\\ell^1$ distance from $p(t)$ is the scalar Poisson tail $\\tau_K(\\lambda)=\\mathbb P(\\operatorname{Pois}(\\lambda)>K)$. If $\\nu t>0$, the budgeted algorithm sets $m=\\lceil\\nu t\\rceil$ and $\\mu=\\nu t/m\\le1$, and uses $R_{\\mu,K}=\\sum_{k=0}^K e^{-\\mu}\\mu^kP^k/k!$. Then $R_{\\mu,K}^m p_0$ is nonnegative and substochastic, and its exact transient $\\ell^1$ error is\n\n$$1-\\left(\\sum_{k=0}^{K}e^{-\\mu}\\frac{\\mu^k}{k!}\\right)^m\\le m\\tau_K(\\mu)\\le mG_K(\\mu).$$\n\nIf a computed vector $\\widehat u$ has a separately certified accumulated arithmetic/algebraic error $E_{\\rm alg}:=\\|\\widehat u-R_{\\mu,K}^mp_0\\|_1$, then $\\|p(t)-\\widehat u\\|_1\\le mG_K(\\mu)+E_{\\rm alg}$. In rounded arithmetic, if $T$ is a validated upper bound for $mG_K(\\mu)$, then $\\|p(t)-\\widehat u\\|_1\\le T+E_{\\rm alg}$. The geometric tail certificate is not obtained by floating-point subtraction from one.",
          "uses": [
            "1.2"
          ]
        }
